# Design Narrative
# Mechanic: Tainted Remedy replaces an opponent's life gain with equal life loss.
# Forcing: Swords to Plowshares is the only spell. Exiling the six-power creature causes exactly six life loss; exiling the smaller one does not.
# AI behavior: The opponent has no responses, and the player must choose which opposing creature receives Swords to Plowshares.
# Failure modes:
#   WIN = Colossal Dreadmaw is exiled and its would-be life gain defeats its controller.
#   LOSE = Grizzly Bears is exiled instead, or Swords is not cast.
#   TIMEOUT = the exile target or replacement did not resolve.
# Card roles:
#   Tainted Remedy — turns the opponent's life gain into the win condition.
#   Swords to Plowshares — exiles a creature and creates the life-gain event.
#   Colossal Dreadmaw — the lethal six-power target.
#   Grizzly Bears — the tempting cheaper target that leaves the opponent alive.
# Protocol path: Cast Swords, choose a creature, exile it, replace life gain with life loss.
[metadata]
Name:The Cure Is Worse
Goal:Win
Turns:1
Difficulty:Medium
Description:Win this turn. The removal spell normally gives your opponent life.

